WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.720
This wearable sensor can track the composition
of your sweat and send the data to your phone.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:11.270
Athletes can use information from sweat to
prevent fatigue before it starts.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:17.560
These four pads change color to measure chloride,
glucose, pH, and lactate.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.289
A channel fills with sweat to gauge water
loss.

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.550
These indicators provide information about
hydration status and electrolyte balance,

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.650
as well as the total amount of water lost
to sweat.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.219
The ability to quickly and easily measure
these things with a phone is a huge improvement

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.179
over the previous, lab-bound technologies
for sweat monitoring.

00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:45.339
The sensor is rugged and flexible enough to
move -- even during strenuous exercise.

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:49.179
It may also have medical uses in the future,
like tracking blood sugar without the need

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:50.870
to collect blood.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:53.990
This smart little sensor is probably the first
thing

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.700
that actually wants to be around your  sweat!

